## Initial Q&A
### In what year and at what event were the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund officially established?
Answer: The foundations for the International Monetary Fund (IMF) and the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development (which later became the World Bank) were laid in July 1944 at the "United Nations Monetary and Financial Conference" in Bretton Woods, New Hampshire. The institutions were officially brought to life on December 27, 1945, when participating nations executed documents to "breathe the breath of life" into them.

Source URL: https://pubdocs.worldbank.org/en/634901541019944926/70-years-prologue.pdf

### Who are the historically recognized founders and key architects responsible for establishing the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund?
Answer: According to the provided source, the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund (IMF) were established in July 1944 based on the ideas of "a trio of key experts – US Treasury Secretary Henry Morganthau, his chief economic advisor Harry Dexter White, and British economist John Maynard Keynes."

Source URL: https://www.brettonwoodsproject.org/2019/01/art-320747/

### Was Dr. Jose Rizal alive during the Bretton Woods Conference in 1944 when the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund were created?
Answer: No, Dr. Jose Rizal was not alive during the Bretton Woods Conference in 1944. According to the provided source, Rizal was executed decades earlier, on December 30, 1896, which is commemorated annually in the Philippines as Rizal Day, "the anniversary of Rizal's 1896 execution at Bagumbayan."

Source URL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rizal_Day

### Do the official founding charters or historical archives of the International Monetary Fund mention Dr. Jose Rizal or Ferdinand Marcos as founders or contributors?
Answer: Based on the provided historical document from the International Monetary Fund, there is no mention of Dr. Jose Rizal or Ferdinand Marcos as founders or contributors of the institution. Instead, the text records that the framework of the IMF was designed by the men at the Bretton Woods conference in 1944, whereas Ferdinand Marcos is only mentioned in the archives in relation to "economic deterioration under dictatorship" and "pervasive corruption" in the Philippines.

Source URL: https://www.imf.org/external/pubs/ft/history/2001/ch01.pdf

### What was the official involvement of the Commonwealth of the Philippines in the establishment of the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund in 1944?
Answer: In 1944, the Philippines was officially involved in the establishment of the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund by being represented as one of the forty-four nations at the Bretton Woods Conference, where the blueprints for both institutions were drawn. Although the Philippines was "still two years away from independence from the United States," it participated in the conference, though the search result notes that "the United States was in command" and "virtually no delegations challenged the United States" during the drafting of these institutions' blueprints.

